<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/fn/VA22-Footnote1.4> a ipbes:Footnote ;
    ipbes:Report ipbes:VA22 ;
    ipbes:SubChapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/VA22-1.4.2> ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Indigenous peoples and local communities (referred as IPLCs) is an umbrella term used internationally by representatives, organizations, and conventions to represent the most culturally diverse segment of the world’s populations (IPBES, 2021). However, it is recognized that in particular contexts and situations it is more appropriate to treat them separately, as it is done in many sections of the assessment." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Footnote1.4" .

